    <string name="settings_sec_source_note">Where the runtime subsystem may look for a Java build, and what it must prove before selecting one.</string>
    <string name="settings_sec_detected_note">Each row is a directory this app measured: its ELF header, its release file, its size. None of it is guessed.</string>
    <string name="settings_sec_catalogue_note">Archives published by the Termux repository with a digest this launcher can verify. Licence: %1$s.</string>
    <string name="settings_sec_heap_note">The value is written into the selected installation\'s JVM arguments; the argument builder clamps what the device can grant.</string>
    <string name="settings_sec_window_note">Written into the installation\'s game arguments as --width and --height.</string>
    <string name="settings_sec_backend_note">Choosing a renderer needs the EGL/GLFW surface, which is not in this build. What can be measured is shown instead.</string>
    <string name="settings_sec_arg_lines_note">The launcher splits these into arguments itself; the model refuses a newline.</string>
    <string name="settings_sec_root_note">The root changes on the next launch: the storage layout is prepared when the engine starts, and reloadConfig does not rebuild it.</string>
    <string name="settings_sec_dirs_note">Each was probed writable when the layout was prepared. A directory that could not be proven is absent rather than listed hopefully.</string>
    <string name="settings_sec_player_note">Authentication is not added yet. Until it lands the launcher holds no player, so no sign-in control is offered here.</string>
    <string name="settings_sec_terms_note">The acknowledgement gates the version download; it is stored as a row, not as a checkbox that forgets itself.</string>
    <string name="settings_sec_build_note">Read from the installed package and the running engine, not from constants copied into a layout.</string>

